  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>(A)&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Cr</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi>Ar</mi></mfenced><mn>3</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>5</mn></msup><mn>4</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></math></p><p>(B) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></math>&nbsp;means the magnetic quantum number may have negative values.</p><p>(C) According to Aufbau principle, orbitals are filled in order of their increasing energies.</p><p>(D) Total nodes <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p>"
